llvm-3.3 backport patch: one store merge per visit of a store (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a function whose chained constant
stores hold more than one mergeable run: DAGCombiner::visitSTORE calls
MergeConsecutiveStores once, as LLVM 3.2 does (its visitSTORE reads
`if (!LegalTypes && MergeConsecutiveStores(ST))`), instead of repeating it
until the visited store is merged (upstream commit 1157e1410c83 of
2012-12-02, "Allow merging multiple store sequences on the same chain",
which the 3.3 release carries). The library region of the executable keeps
only the lowest run of each walk merged: hkpConstraintInfo's four counts
at 0x7a020 (+0 and +4 one 8-byte store, +8 and +0xc apart), the spring
forces at 0x17afe0 and hkpPositionConstraintMotor's constructor at 0x82430
(the forces merged, tau, damping and the two recovery velocities apart, in
source order). docs/DECISIONS.md D27 holds the measurement.

--- a/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp
@@ -8524,21 +8524,8 @@
 
   // Only perform this optimization before the types are legal, because we
   // don't want to perform this optimization on every DAGCombine invocation.
-  if (!LegalTypes) {
-    bool EverChanged = false;
-
-    do {
-      // There can be multiple store sequences on the same chain.
-      // Keep trying to merge store sequences until we are unable to do so
-      // or until we merge the last store on the chain.
-      bool Changed = MergeConsecutiveStores(ST);
-      EverChanged |= Changed;
-      if (!Changed) break;
-    } while (ST->getOpcode() != ISD::DELETED_NODE);
-
-    if (EverChanged)
-      return SDValue(N, 0);
-  }
+  if (!LegalTypes && MergeConsecutiveStores(ST))
+    return SDValue(N, 0);
 
   return ReduceLoadOpStoreWidth(N);
 }
